         - Template fetch directly DB se nahi karte — latency badh jaayegi. 

           Templates read-heavy hoti hain, write-heavy nahi. Isliye application aur DB ke beech Redis as distributed cache use karte hain — koi local/instance-level cache nahi,
           consistency aur simplicity ke liye.

           Fetch flow:
 
             L1: Template Redis (shared)          → HIT 1-3ms
             L2: Template DB (source of truth)    → HIT 10-50ms
             └─→ SET Redis (TTL 5min)          ← first request pe populate

        — Local cache isliye nahi rakhte kyunki us case me har template update pe saare instances ka local cache invalidate karna padega — jiske liye event-based invalidation (Kafka) chahiye,
          jaise rate limiter design me kiya tha. Template update ke waqt ye invalidation fail ho sakti hai, aur templates compliance-adherent hote hain — to stale template trigger hona breach hai.
          Isliye Redis as shared cache use karte hain:

        — Template Service (separate service):
           → Template create, update, delete karne ke liye ek alag Template Service hai.
           → Create: Template Service DB me template insert karti hai → Redis me entry create karti hai → TTL set karti hai (5 min).
           → Update: Template Service DB me template update karti hai → Redis me bhi template update karti hai. Yahan invalidate (delete) nahi, update karte hain — kyunki invalidation se thundering 
             herd problem aa sakti hai. Update karne se har instance ko ko Redis se hi latest template milta hai.

        — Agar Redis SET fail ho jaye (rare — network issue) , to TTL as a safety net hai: TTL expire hone pe next request DB se fresh template fetch karke Redis repopulate kar degi. Aur kyunki sabhi instances 
          same Redis se read hain, fix bhi same time pe hota hai — inconsistent state nahi banti. Templates rare update hote hain, to agar Redis update kabhi miss bhi ho jaye, to manual invalidate/update bhi 
          possible hai — koi critical issue nahi. Isliye decision: Redis-only rakhte hain — simple, consistent, compliance-safe. 1-3ms local cache savings ke liye compliance risk lena worth nahi.



