      h) Channel-wise Event Publishing & Processing

         - Ab Instance 1 producer ki tarah act karta hai aur sirf applicable channels ke respective Kafka topics (email_events, sms_events, push_events) mein channel-specific payloads/events publish karta hai.

         - Har topic ka apna independent Consumer Group hota hai — email-workers, sms-workers, push-workers. Har Consumer Group ke andar multiple consumers (workers) ho sakte hain, jo respective topic ke partitions
           se events parallelly consume aur process karte hain. Isse overall event processing throughput improve hota hai.

         - In consumers ki responsibility respective channel ke payloads ko corresponding external client/aggregator tak forward karna hoti hai via synchronous HTTP POST API call, taaki user ko applicable channels
           ke through Notification deliver ho sake.

         - Worker aggregator se success acknowledgement ka configured timeout tak synchronously wait karta hai. Agar configured timeout ke andar success acknowledgement nahi milta, toh worker configured retry
           policy ke according request retry karta hai. Retries ke beech Exponential Backoff + Jitter apply hota hai. Configured maximum retry attempts exhaust hone ke baad bhi request fail hoti hai, toh worker
           failed event ko us channel ke corresponding DLT mein publish kar deta hai (email_events_dlt, sms_events_dlt, push_events_dlt).

         - Aggregator se success acknowledgement (200 OK ya 202 Accepted) receive hone ke baad, worker apne respective Kafka topic ke partition ka offset commit karta hai. Iske baad woh next available message
           consume karke process karta hai.

           ## Important Nuance — 202 Accepted ≠ Delivered to User
              → 202 Accepted ka matlab sirf itna hai ki aggregator ne message receive kar liya hai ("maine SMS/Email/Push receive kar liya hai, main process karunga") — ye guarantee nahi ki
                message user tak pahunch gaya. Actual delivery ki tracking webhook ke through asynchronously hoti hai. Isi wajah se worker 202 Accepted aane pe hi offset commit kar deta hai, 
                actual delivery ka wait nahi karta — kyunki provider ne message ki responsibility le li hai.

